# Normalise text to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Measured before this file existed (597 tracked files, core.autocrlf=false):
# 592 were already LF and exactly five Markdown files carried CRLF --
# docs/CHANGELOG.md, docs/observability/14-auto-remediation.md,
# docs/modules/M-12-canvas-editor-frontend.md,
# docs/observability/11-phased-rollout.md and
# crates/ada-m12-canvas-editor/CRDT.md. So this is a small, reviewable change,
# not the repo-wide renormalisation it was assumed might be.
#
# `text=auto` rather than `text`: Git decides per file whether the content is
# text, so binary assets are left untouched without needing an explicit list
# of extensions to maintain.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text` alone: with only `text`, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true would still write CRLF back into the working tree, and
# this repository tracks ten .sh files that break under CRLF. The working-tree
# guarantee matters as much as the repository one.
* text=auto eol=lf